@database "image_gen"
@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: image_gen.guide 1.0 (24.11.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "Image Generation"
@{h1}Image Generation

The @{tt}image_gen@{utt} plugin gives agents sandboxed access to cloud image
generation and editing models configured under
@{tt}llm_system.image_models@{utt} and @{tt}llm_system.image_profiles@{utt}.
Each call writes the generated image to disk inside the instance's write
sandbox and can attach a preview so a vision-capable model inspects the
result directly and refines it with @{tt}reference_images@{utt}.

Two tools, no hooks and no panel. Multiple instances can run side by side
with different sandboxes and profile allowlists.

@{code}
For agents and developers
  @{"  generate  " link generate}
  @{"  list_profiles  " link list_profiles}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}
@{body}
@endnode

@node generate "generate"
@{h1}generate

Calls @{tt}create_image_from_profile@{utt} for the selected profile, saves the
image atomically to @{tt}output_path@{utt} (converting formats via Pillow when
the file extension differs from the model's MIME type), and optionally
attaches a preview image.

@{table}
Parameter | Meaning
prompt | required; description of the image to create or edit instruction
output_path | required; target file path inside @{tt}output_directories@{utt}
profile | image profile from @{tt}llm_system.image_profiles@{utt} (optional when @{tt}default_profile@{utt} is set)
reference_images | optional list of file paths inside @{tt}input_directories@{utt} for editing or consistency
aspect_ratio | optional aspect ratio (e.g. @{tt}1:1@{utt}, @{tt}16:9@{utt}, @{tt}4:3@{utt})
image_size | optional resolution tier (e.g. @{tt}1K@{utt}, @{tt}2K@{utt}, @{tt}4K@{utt})
seed | optional integer seed (where supported by the provider)
attach_preview | @{tt}true@{utt} (default): attach the generated image to the tool result when under the request size limit
@{body}

Returns @{tt}status: "success"@{utt} with @{tt}path@{utt}, @{tt}width@{utt},
@{tt}height@{utt}, @{tt}bytes@{utt}, @{tt}mime_type@{utt}, @{tt}profile@{utt},
@{tt}model@{utt}, optional @{tt}text@{utt} (when the model returns commentary),
and @{tt}not_attached@{utt} if the preview exceeded the attachment limit.
@endnode

@node list_profiles "list_profiles"
@{h1}list_profiles

Lists the image generation profiles allowed on this instance with their
@{tt}description@{utt}, @{tt}provider@{utt}, @{tt}model@{utt}, default
@{tt}aspect_ratio@{utt} / @{tt}image_size@{utt}, and @{tt}is_default@{utt}.
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

@{h2}Tool descriptions and errors

The schema lists the allowed profile names as an enum when at least one
profile is configured, and makes @{tt}profile@{utt} optional when
@{tt}default_profile@{utt} is set. Validation errors (path outside sandbox,
missing reference file, unsupported capability such as @{tt}reference_images@{utt}
or @{tt}seed@{utt} on a provider that lacks it) return
@{tt}{"status": "error", "error": "..."}@{utt} before any API call.

@{h2}Token and cache effect

Append-only: each call returns one tool result. When @{tt}attach_preview@{utt}
is @{tt}true@{utt}, the generated image is attached via the multimodal tool
channel (frozen by content hash so overwriting the path later does not
invalidate earlier turns in the prompt cache).

@{h2}Known gaps

@{bullet}One image per call on current providers (@{tt}gemini_image@{utt},
@{tt}openrouter_image@{utt}).
@{bullet}@{tt}file_checkpoints@{utt} counts @{tt}image_gen/generate@{utt} as
an untracked write rather than snapshotting previous bytes at
@{tt}output_path@{utt}.
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

Configure image models and profiles under @{tt}llm_system@{utt} (for example
in @{tt}config/llm.yaml@{utt} or @{tt}config/llm_openrouter.yaml@{utt}):

@{code yaml}
llm_system:
  image_models:
    gemini-nano-banana-2.1:
      provider: gemini_image
      model: gemini-nano-banana-2.1
  image_profiles:
    nano-banana:
      model_ref: gemini-nano-banana-2.1
      description: "Google Nano Banana 2.1 (direct Gemini API)"
@{body}

Then configure an instance in @{tt}config/plugins.yaml@{utt} or an agent's
@{tt}tools.yaml@{utt}:

@{table}
Key | Default | Meaning
output_directories | data/image_gen | write sandbox (PathSandbox); empty refuses all writes
input_directories | same as output_directories | read-only sandbox for @{tt}reference_images@{utt}
profiles | all configured | allowlist of @{tt}llm_system.image_profiles@{utt}
default_profile | none | profile used when @{tt}generate@{utt} omits @{tt}profile@{utt}
max_reference_size_mb | 15.0 | maximum size per reference image in MiB
@{body}
@endnode
